  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "quickFacts",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/6qkuko5edszpeouygearvg6ca9e5y1-rdw8w",
      "html": "<p>From the Betta unimaculata complex. IUCN Red List: Endangered (a very high risk of extinction in the wild). Wild caught Betta patoti from Tanah Grogot.</p><ul><li>Maximum size: 3.5 inches (about 9 cm)</li><li>TDS: ~60–100</li><li>pH: ~5.0–7.0</li><li>Temperature: 72–82°F (22–28°C)</li><li>Breeding: mouthbrooder</li></ul>"
    },
    {
      "key": "beforeYouBuy",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/6qkuko5edszpeouygearvg6ca9e5y1-rdw8w",
      "html": "<p>Be sure to have the habitat ready before purchase.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/6qkuko5edszpeouygearvg6ca9e5y1-rdw8w",
      "html": "<p>TDS ~60–100, pH ~5.0–7.0. Temperature: 72–82°F (22–28°C); they prefer cooler temperatures, but higher temperatures induce coloration and breeding behaviours.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "diet",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/6qkuko5edszpeouygearvg6ca9e5y1-rdw8w",
      "html": "<p>Carnivorous. Currently fed live, frozen and dried foods: blackworms, frozen bloodworms and pellets.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/6qkuko5edszpeouygearvg6ca9e5y1-rdw8w",
      "html": "<p>Like many of the species in this complex, with the largest bettas, they can be aggressive. We recommend that they be kept in a species-only tank as they can eat anything that fits in their big mouth.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "dimorphism",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/6qkuko5edszpeouygearvg6ca9e5y1-rdw8w",
      "html": "<p>They have a brown base body with blue iridescence on the opercular cheeks, body and tails; females have less iridescence. Both males and females can occasionally show tiger-like stripes on the sides of the body. Fully grown adult males have longer ventral fins.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "bwaquatics",
      "sourceUrl": "https://bwaquatics.com/products/6qkuko5edszpeouygearvg6ca9e5y1-rdw8w",
      "html": "<p>Mouthbrooder.</p>"
    }
  ],
